# Organization-default CODEOWNERS.
#
# This file lives in the special `.github` repo. GitHub uses a repo's OWN .github/CODEOWNERS first;
# if a repo has none, GitHub falls back to THIS org-default. Keep teams here generic; per-repo repos
# may add a more specific CODEOWNERS.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <owner> [<owner> ...]   (last matching pattern wins)
# Owners must have write access. Required-review enforcement is configured in the org ruleset
# (see docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md).

# Default owners for everything in the org.
*                               @aircloud/maintainers

# Platform / CI ownership — the reusable workflows and anything that affects every repo.
/.github/                       @aircloud/platform @aircloud/security
/.github/workflows/             @aircloud/platform @aircloud/security
/examples/                      @aircloud/platform

# Security-sensitive governance files require the security team.
/SECURITY.md                    @aircloud/security
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md             @aircloud/maintainers @aircloud/community
/GOVERNANCE.md                  @aircloud/maintainers
/.github/dependabot.yml         @aircloud/platform @aircloud/security

# Documentation.
/docs/                          @aircloud/platform @aircloud/docs
*.md                            @aircloud/docs

# AI assistant configuration — kept in sync with real repo commands.
/CLAUDE.md                      @aircloud/platform
/AGENTS.md                      @aircloud/platform
/.github/copilot-instructions.md @aircloud/platform
/.cursor/                       @aircloud/platform
